    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 3,
        "sourceEnd": 409,
        "text": "Hi everyone, thanks for coming to the community garden meeting. I know it's a busy time, but we have a few important issues to discuss. First, the water supply. As you know, the tap near the greenhouse has been broken for two weeks. If we don't fix it soon, the plants in that area will suffer. I've contacted the council, but they say it's not their responsibility. So we need to think about alternatives.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "b4eac85e230aa52e1e5ae85becedea572c98018f4042ed52242b2348c0667ffc",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 414,
        "sourceEnd": 673,
        "text": "Excuse me, could I say something? I'm Sarah, I live on Elm Street. I think we should ask the local hardware store for help. If they donate some materials, we could repair the tap ourselves. My neighbour is a plumber, and he might be willing to give us advice.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "10919090dd2c41f4d70c03d2656b3c84bf468f97681b0ec7d11b3302a16125fe",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 678,
        "sourceEnd": 832,
        "text": "That's a good suggestion, Sarah. But we should also consider the cost. If we buy the parts ourselves, it might be expensive. Does anyone have other ideas?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "f0d994103fe805835a87abf379496d62e5943c17f17c3ccd9a17361637981bfa",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 837,
        "sourceEnd": 998,
        "text": "Well, what if we organise a small fundraising event? A bake sale or something. If we raise enough money, we can pay for the repairs and maybe even buy new tools.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "d8ccf20689f883cf499e451b7a7fff031e2f97bef67c752f225af3e65f266b99",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1003,
        "sourceEnd": 1188,
        "text": "I like that idea. But we need to be careful about timing. The summer festival is coming up, and many people will be away. If we hold the event too late, we might not get enough support.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "a51c2f709f4ffaf16230b34aab067254252b70d503ddd50beba31950eca07ce8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1193,
        "sourceEnd": 1319,
        "text": "That's true. How about next Saturday? It's short notice, but if we spread the word quickly, we could still get a good turnout.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "2acc033a7541c3062203bbd770b42c6671dda35f88ea4ef951921145de418648",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1324,
        "sourceEnd": 1419,
        "text": "Next Saturday could work. Let's put it to a vote. All in favour of the bake sale next Saturday?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "85408ef356cc7a07b13ceee5bc20f194ab11978198ccc69c4472b0dcb4b22296",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "narrator",
        "speaker": "Narrator",
        "sourceStart": 1422,
        "sourceEnd": 1452,
        "text": "(General murmurs of agreement)",
        "boundary": "paragraph",
        "voice": "en-US-BrianNeural",
        "textHash": "8a5524dc0f72419267529d43ef0288f2a3d4df5e6e5ac18e56e52470d2088b42",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1457,
        "sourceEnd": 1640,
        "text": "Great, it's decided. Now, the second issue: the compost heap. Some residents have complained about the smell. If we don't manage it better, we might get more complaints. Any thoughts?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "fc136b0fdb641ec1c525d86a4755401b33e59080112b9317ad527dab9543111b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1645,
        "sourceEnd": 1766,
        "text": "We could cover it with a layer of soil. That usually helps. And if we turn it more regularly, it shouldn't smell as much.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "3220ba0a1a668b372b3ecb5eb5b7543d575c5b2163954771c2c3f1003dccc5d7",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1771,
        "sourceEnd": 1984,
        "text": "Good point. I'll add that to the list. Finally, the notice board. It's looking a bit old. If we have time, we could repaint it. But that's not urgent. Let's focus on the tap and the compost first. Thanks everyone.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "0795459de2b665d90481b36fc73b9d1739089b1fcf34d7c96c5d2c125e70b1aa",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      }
    ]
  },
